From: Alberto Garcia <berto@igalia.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:57:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] gtk/WebKitWebViewBase.cpp:3849:23: error: no viable
 overloaded '=' https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=332157

Unreviewed build fix.

Drop the type reference indication (i.e.  turn "auto&" into "auto")
because the ::platformImage() function returns a Skia sk_sp<T> smart
pointer by value.

The same fix was applied in the main branch in 319114@main as part of
a larger change.

* Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitWebViewBase.cpp:
(webkitWebViewBaseSetCursor):

Canonical link: https://commits.webkit.org/317695.778@webkitglib/2.54
---
 Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitWebViewBase.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitWebViewBase.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitWebViewBase.cpp
index 7646e921..7173f704 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitWebViewBase.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitWebViewBase.cpp
@@ -3820,7 +3820,7 @@ void webkitWebViewBaseSetCursor(WebKitWebViewBase* webViewBase, const Cursor& cu
 
     auto cursorScale = cursor.imageScaleFactor();
     IntPoint effectiveHotSpot = determineHotSpot(cursor.image().get(), cursor.hotSpot()).scaled(1 / cursorScale);
-    auto& platformImage = nativeImage->platformImage();
+    auto platformImage = nativeImage->platformImage();
 
 #if USE(GTK4)
     if (cursorScale != 1) {
